TASK-191.2 runtime harness: links from other apps routed by Link
Routes. Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. It logs, for every
application(_:open:), the raw sender attributes of the Apple Event being
handled (spid, addr, from), what NSRunningApplication says about the sender,
the resolved sender, the route decision, the placement and the windows
(recent first), and dumps every window's space, selection and tabs on a
"dump" command. Phase 1 seeds spaces Work, Personal, Other and routes
(domainIs work.test/personal.test/other.test -> those spaces; contains
"secret" -> Private window; app-only com.detourbrowser.verify.sender-a ->
Personal; domainIs mru.test -> Most Recent Space) and opens a window on Work
and one on Personal in front of the launch window. Commands are appended to
$DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR/cmd-<phase>.txt: dump <label>, default <space name |
anything else = Most Recent Space>, activate, restore.

SAFETY: the Debug build has the production bundle ID (com.detourbrowser.mac).
`open URL`, `open -a <debug path> URL` without -n, or NSWorkspace without a
new instance can hand the link to the user's running /Applications/Detour.app.
Safe deliveries used here:
  1. sendurl (below): a kAEGetURL built with
     NSAppleEventDescriptor(processIdentifier:) and sent with sendEvent; it
     refuses unless the PID's executable is .derived/.../Detour.app, and
     refuses when AEDeterminePermissionToAutomateTarget(GURL, ask: false) is
     not noErr (never prompts).
  2. `open -n -a <debug app> --env ... URL...`: a new instance gets the URLs.
  3. A copy of the Debug app with its own bundle ID
     (PlistBuddy CFBundleIdentifier com.detourbrowser.verify.debugcopy,
     re-signed ad hoc with only get-task-allow), then plain `open -a <copy>`
     and NSWorkspace.open(_:withApplicationAt:) from small LSUIElement apps
     (LSOpen-a/-b, bundle IDs com.detourbrowser.verify.sender-a/-b): nothing
     can resolve to production. Unregister it afterwards
     (lsregister -u <copy>) and delete its defaults domain.
Production's window list (CGWindowList names) was compared before and after
each LaunchServices delivery: unchanged.

    SP=<scratch>; mkdir -p $SP/out
    git apply docs/harness/task191-2-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    APP=.derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1912 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=1 $APP &
    sendurl <pid> https://work.test/1          # one URL per event
    sendurl <pid> --list <url> <url> ...       # one event, a list direct object
    git apply -R docs/harness/task191-2-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Results (2026-10-25):
- Phase 1 (sendurl, Detour inactive): work.test -> the Work window, brought
  to the front of Detour's windows; other.test (no window) -> the most recent
  normal window switched to Other; secret -> a new Private window, then a
  second secret link (a normal window in front) -> a tab in that Private
  window; unmatched or mru.test with Detour inactive -> today's path: no key
  window, so a new window each time; with Detour active -> a tab in the key
  window's space; Default = Personal -> the Personal window. One GURL whose
  direct object is a list of four URLs reached application(_:open:) as one
  call and each URL routed on its own (Work switch, Personal window, Other
  window, Private window).
- sendurl's sender: spid = its PID, NSRunningApplication nil -> no sender. The
  same binary exec'd from inside an .app bundle is also unknown to
  NSRunningApplication (not launched through LaunchServices).
- open -n -a <debug> URL1 URL2 URL3: the URLs arrive after
  applicationDidFinishLaunching, one per call; two carried spid = the `open`
  process (no bundle ID); the first URL arrived with no current Apple Event
  (currentAppleEvent nil), so no sender for the link that launches Detour.
- LSOpen-a -> running copy: spid = LSOpen-a's PID, bundle ID
  com.detourbrowser.verify.sender-a -> the app-only route (Personal); LSOpen-b
  -> the Default; LSOpen-a with work.test -> Work (the URL route is first);
  two URLs from one NSWorkspace.open -> two events, each routed.
- `open -a <copy> URL` from the shell: spid = `open`, no bundle ID.
- AEDeterminePermissionToAutomateTarget(GURL) returned noErr for sendurl in
  two runs and -1744 (would need consent) in one, also for sendurl apps
  launched by LaunchServices: nothing was sent then.

--- sendurl.swift ---
    // Sends a kAEGetURL Apple Event to ONE process, by PID, after checking that the
    // PID is the Debug build under .derived (never /Applications/Detour.app).
    // usage: sendurl <pid> [--list] <url>...
    import AppKit
    
    let args = Array(CommandLine.arguments.dropFirst())
    guard args.count >= 2, let pid = pid_t(args[0]) else { print("usage: sendurl <pid> [--list] <url>..."); exit(2) }
    var urls = Array(args.dropFirst())
    let asList = urls.first == "--list"
    if asList { urls.removeFirst() }
    
    guard let target = NSRunningApplication(processIdentifier: pid), let exe = target.executableURL?.path else {
        print("REFUSE: no running application with pid \(pid)"); exit(3)
    }
    let allowed = "/Users/tma/Projects/browser/MyBrowser/.derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour"
    print("target pid=\(pid) exe=\(exe) bundleID=\(target.bundleIdentifier ?? "nil")")
    guard exe == allowed else { print("REFUSE: target is not the Debug build"); exit(4) }
    let me = ProcessInfo.processInfo.processIdentifier
    let mine = NSRunningApplication(processIdentifier: me)
    print("sender pid=\(me) bundleID=\(mine?.bundleIdentifier ?? "nil") Bundle.main=\(Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier ?? "nil")")
    
    let targetDesc = NSAppleEventDescriptor(processIdentifier: pid)
    // Permission probe first, never asking: a GURL needing consent is not sent.
    let perm = AEDeterminePermissionToAutomateTarget(targetDesc.aeDesc, AEEventClass(kInternetEventClass), AEEventID(kAEGetURL), false)
    print("AEDeterminePermissionToAutomateTarget(GURL, ask=false) = \(perm)")
    guard perm == noErr else { print("REFUSE: sending would need consent (\(perm))"); exit(5) }
    
    func send(_ direct: NSAppleEventDescriptor) {
        let event = NSAppleEventDescriptor(eventClass: AEEventClass(kInternetEventClass), eventID: AEEventID(kAEGetURL),
                                           targetDescriptor: targetDesc, returnID: AEReturnID(kAutoGenerateReturnID),
                                           transactionID: AETransactionID(kAnyTransactionID))
        event.setParam(direct, forKeyword: keyDirectObject)
        do {
            _ = try event.sendEvent(options: [.noReply], timeout: 5)
            print("sent \(direct)")
        } catch {
            print("send failed: \(error)")
        }
    }
    if asList {
        let list = NSAppleEventDescriptor.list()
        for (i, u) in urls.enumerated() { list.insert(NSAppleEventDescriptor(string: u), at: i + 1) }
        send(list)
    } else {
        for u in urls { send(NSAppleEventDescriptor(string: u)) }
    }

--- lsopen.swift ---
    // Opens URLs through LaunchServices in the app at <appPath>, which must NOT be
    // com.detourbrowser.mac. mode "new" = createsNewApplicationInstance.
    // usage: lsopen <appPath> <new|running> <outDir> <phase> <url>...
    import AppKit
    let a = Array(CommandLine.arguments.dropFirst())
    let app = URL(fileURLWithPath: a[0]); let mode = a[1]; let outDir = a[2]; let phase = a[3]
    let urls = a.dropFirst(4).compactMap(URL.init(string:))
    guard let bid = Bundle(url: app)?.bundleIdentifier, bid != "com.detourbrowser.mac" || mode == "new" else {
        print("REFUSE: target bundle \(Bundle(url: app)?.bundleIdentifier ?? "nil")"); exit(4)
    }
    let cfg = NSWorkspace.OpenConfiguration()
    cfg.createsNewApplicationInstance = (mode == "new")
    cfg.activates = false
    if mode == "new" { cfg.environment = ["DETOUR_DATA_DIR": "DetourVerify1912", "DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR": outDir, "DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE": phase] }
    print("lsopen pid=\(ProcessInfo.processInfo.processIdentifier) bundle=\(Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier ?? "nil") target=\(bid) mode=\(mode) urls=\(urls)")
    NSWorkspace.shared.open(urls, withApplicationAt: app, configuration: cfg) { running, error in
        print("opened in pid=\(running?.processIdentifier ?? -1) exe=\(running?.executableURL?.path ?? "nil") error=\(String(describing: error))")
    }
    RunLoop.main.run(until: Date().addingTimeInterval(6))   // stay alive while the target reads the sender
    print("exit"); exit(0)

